 - `writeReport` accepts `format` argument to enable additional exporters (HTML, CSV) later.
 - CLI parsing accommodates further evaluation subcommands (e.g., `frai eval bias`).
 
+## Thresholds (Gate for CI)
+- `generateReport` accepts an optional `thresholds` object (e.g., `{ exact_match: 0.9, toxicity: 0.95 }`).
+- CLI `frai eval` accepts repeated `--threshold <metric>=<min>` options (e.g., `--threshold exact_match=0.9 --threshold toxicity=0.95`).
+- A threshold passes when metric score >= minimum; metrics with no score fail their thresholds.
+- Exit 1 if any threshold fails, 0 if all pass. Thresholds are reported either way.
+- JSON reports include top-level `passed` boolean and `thresholds` list with `{ metric, min, score, passed }` entries.
+- Markdown reports include a "Thresholds" section showing PASS/FAIL for each.
+- Malformed thresholds or unknown metrics trigger exit 2 with descriptive error (listing valid metric ids).
+
 ## Follow-up Tasks
 1. Integrate real toxicity/bias models once provider abstraction is implemented (Phase 0 → Providers milestone).
 2. Extend datasets loader to support configurable schema mapping.
